        },
        "question": {
          ":question/problem": "A curve is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx={t}^{2}-t+1,\\,y={t}^{3}+{t}^{2}-16t,\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty .\n$$\n\nDetermine the values of $t$ at which the tangent to the curve is horizontal. Give exact answers.\n\nIn **ascending order**, the tangent to the curve is horizontal at $t=$\n{{field-1}}\nand $t=$\n{{field-2}}.",
          ":question/answer-fields": [
            {
              ":answer-field/key": "field-1",
